  "FLINK-19522": {
    "jira_id": "FLINK-19522",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Add ability to set auto commit on jdbc driver from Table/SQL API",
    "description": "When I tried to stream data from postgres via the JDBC source connector in the SQL api, it was loading the entirety of the table into memory before starting streaming. This is due to the postgres JDBC driver requiring the autoCommit flag to be set to false for streaming to take place.\r\n\r\nFLINK-12198 provided the means to do this with the JDBCInputSource, but this did not extend to the SQL description. This option should be added.\r\n\r\nTo reproduce, create a very large table and try to read it in with the SQL api. You will see a large spike of memory usage and no data streaming, and then it will start all at once. I will attach a couple of graphs before and after I made a patch to the code myself to set auto-commit.",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "a55035fb0a9a2aecec9e1469f30a6f991e9e9504",
